## Last text from previous session

2D425C215C`, v0.5.5, all RULE-4 proven)

1. **Throttle mask bug** (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` ~9300): the v0.3.136 "every 100th unlock" log-force throttle used `& 99` — a bitwise AND passing 8 of every 128 values (every ~16th). Fixed to `& 127`. ftrace-proven: xfs_log_force 1650 → ~365 calls/node/run.
2. **Adaptive yield-quantum cap 32 → 512** (`mxfs_ag_yield_quantum` default): eager sync drains ~150 → ~50/run. With fix 1: 2n walls 4356/5300 → 3534/4492 (test1/test2). A/B-proved quantum=32 was NOT the cause of the slow-drain stall (worse at 32).
3. **THE STALL ROOT (stack-sample proven)**: intermittent 20-30s one-node stall = eager drain's `xfs_buf_delwri_submit` sleeping in `xfs_buf_wait_unpin` **with the buffer lock held** after concurrent creates re-logged (re-pinned) the hot cluster/AGI buf into a newer CIL seq that nothing pushes until the 30s log worker; all other tasks convoy on `xfs_buf_lock` (316+317 samples on test2's 30.7s run). Fix: new `xfs_buf_delwri_submit_nopinwait()` (pal/linux/xfs_buf.c, declared xfs_buf.h) — skip pinned bufs without holding locks, submit+iowait the rest, sync log force, retry (10-round bound). Wired into `mxfs_dlm_ag_drain_alloc_buflist`. **Verified: 5 consecutive 4-node rounds zero stalls (was ~1-in-2 at 19-30s); criterion run had no stall in any stage.**
4. **Instr-gated heavy write-path probes** (pal/linux/xfs_buf.c): P133 (sync disk read per inode-cluster write w/ dir dinode), P-DIR-LEAF-CLOBBER (FUA read per leaf write), P-DIRWR (8000-line dmesg spam that wraps the ring and blinded diagnosis). P124/P122 preventers untouched (P122 suppression already hardcoded off per sess23).
5. **Parallel publish drain** (`mxfs_dlm_publish_unpublished`): one peer BAST used to serialize ~9000 unclaimed file slots × 2ms through the ordered bast wq (8845 inode_lock calls observed). Now fans out over 16 `system_unbound_wq` workers (>32 backlog), waits for completion; per-inode clear-then-acquire semantics preserved. P25-PUB probe added (capped).

### New diagnostic tooling (in tree per RULE 3)
- `scripts/diag_stacksample.sh` — off-CPU /proc/pid/stack sampler over the parallel rsync; **this is what cracked the stall**.
- `scripts/diag_funcgraph.sh` — funcgraph w/ tracing_thresh (was empty during stalls; sampler superseded it).
- `scripts/diag_vnop_profile.sh` — added `MXFS_SET_PARAMS` post-mount module-param injection.

